From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linshengwei.lin <>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep Windows Error Reporting enabled

Do not temporarily disable WER during libuv initialization: concurrent graphics
initialization can save that state and restore it after the host enables WER.
Keep suppression of critical-error and OpenFile dialogs.

diff --git a/deps/uv/src/win/core.c b/deps/uv/src/win/core.c
index 73f26c68..439ca701 100644
--- a/deps/uv/src/win/core.c
+++ b/deps/uv/src/win/core.c
@@ -177,9 +177,11 @@ void uv__wake_all_loops(void) {
 }
 
 static void uv__init(void) {
-  /* Tell Windows that we will handle critical errors. */
-  SetErrorMode(SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS | SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX |
-               SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX);
+  /* Suppress critical-error dialogs without disabling Windows Error Reporting.
+   * Graphics initialization may concurrently save and restore the error mode;
+   * setting SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX even temporarily can leave WER disabled.
+   */
+  SetErrorMode(SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS | SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX);
 
   /* Tell the CRT to not exit the application when an invalid parameter is
    * passed. The main issue is that invalid FDs will trigger this behavior.
